      "name": "food_taste_quality",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.62,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Taste is a core theme distinguishing sentiment. But YLP-0001 mentions food items with no taste descriptor yet yields 'delicious', and YLP-0003 yields 'excellent' from 'Very good pizza' which is defensible; the 'delicious' inference is weakly grounded, indicating a tendency to project positive taste onto positive reviews without textual warrant."
    },
    {
      "name": "food_freshness",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
      "source_groundedness": 0.5,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Freshness is a plausible theme, but many 'fresh' values appear invented: YLP-0001 and YLP-0003 never comment on freshness yet both are labeled 'fresh', suggesting fabricated positives correlated with sentiment rather than reading the text."
    },
    {
      "name": "portion_size",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.68,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Portion size is a distinct, useful axis. YLP-0003 'small' is well-grounded from the smallest-pie discussion. However YLP-0001 'generous' has no textual basis, an unwarranted inference."
    },
    {
      "name": "food_freshness_issue",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.2,
      "source_groundedness": 0.5,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Near-duplicate of food_freshness (nearly identical value distributions and identical per-row values in samples); adds essentially no new analytical leverage. Shares the same fabricated-'fresh' groundedness problems."
    },
    {
      "name": "portion_size_satisfaction",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.25,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Largely redundant with portion_size, using the same value vocabulary (generous/adequate/small) rather than a distinct satisfaction judgment; a mere restatement offering little new axis. Groundedness mirrors portion_size, including the unsupported 'generous' on YLP-0001."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.6,
  "source_groundedness": 0.6,
  "rationale": "The columns target real theme axes (service, taste, freshness, portion) that are directly relevant to comparing positive vs negative sentiment, giving genuine grouping leverage. However two columns (food_freshness_issue, portion_size_satisfaction) are near-duplicates of earlier columns and add little. Groundedness is undermined by a systematic tendency to emit positive descriptors (delicious, fresh, generous) on positive-labeled reviews even when the source text is silent, as seen on YLP-0001 and partly YLP-0003, which is a hallucination pattern rather than correct 'not_present' behavior."
